  "notes": [
    "Actual Baka runtime v1 revealed C++ no-DLC sprite replacement, black-baked JIS research title, inline text colours, dark dedicated chrome and legacy BSM white body fonts.",
    "Obsolete deployment rows retain a warm cream/copper warning appearance, distinct from normal white rows. Source alpha holes and frame count are retained.",
    "Two construction GUI copies regain the exact native start_construction_entry repair number child; this is a required engine contract repair, separate from pure theme reference changes.",
    "Runtime v1 requires white glyph sources on navy officer/research/deployment headings; black-baked JIS atlases cannot be made white by tint. Original dark pictograms in captured-commanders/agency creation/focus search remain, so only their captions are white. Inline palette is darkened only in light-surface font clones.",
    "Runtime v2: politics national_spirit caption sits on the now-silver NoDLC face, so black. Captured amount stays in a white-font family to preserve bright H on its green picture button. Light palette must INSERT missing W/g codes as well as replace existing keys; native font palettes often omit them.",
    "Runtime v2 diplomacy mid-panel chrome is static GFX_diplo_upper_diplo_bg/nat_spirits_bg/leader_frame (no C++ variant literals). All three are neutral frame surfaces; political chart overlay and brown focus artwork remain. Its focus label is white. Trade C++ neutral numeric colours require the existing black-baked jis16_b numeric family as a tint-independent luminance cap; glyph pixels are 66/133 grey, so semantic red/green tint is retained rather than becoming uncoloured black. Confirm visually before claiming PASS."
  ],
